# Firebase web app config for the Vercel deployment (dev project: snapspare-edcc1).
#
# Safe to commit: these are Firebase's client-side identifiers, not secrets —
# they ship in every browser's JS bundle regardless. Actual access control is
# enforced by firestore.rules / storage.rules and App Check, not by hiding
# this file. See apps/web/.env (gitignored) for the local-dev copy of the
# same values; keep both in sync if the Firebase web app config changes.
#
# Deliberately NOT carried over from apps/web/.env:
# - VITE_USE_EMULATORS / VITE_USE_AUTH_EMULATOR: this is a real deployment,
#   not a local emulator session.
# - VITE_APPCHECK_DEBUG_TOKEN: a debug token bypasses App Check entirely —
#   must never ship in a deployed bundle.
#
# VITE_RECAPTCHA_ENTERPRISE_SITE_KEY: a reCAPTCHA Enterprise WEBSITE/SCORE key
# (Google Cloud Console > Security > reCAPTCHA Enterprise), registered against
# Firebase App Check for this web app (Firebase console > App Check), and
# restricted to snap-spare-web.vercel.app. When the production domain changes,
# add the new domain to this key's allowed domains too (GCP console >
# reCAPTCHA Enterprise > this key > edit) or App Check will start rejecting
# requests from the new domain.
VITE_RECAPTCHA_ENTERPRISE_SITE_KEY=6Lc074QtAAAAAHy3-y1UD4C2sByZ8E1IWl4Zsu5_
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyAm011n5I9EwHX7Vuv8BeHwb_WMymeLgqA
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=snapspare-edcc1.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=snapspare-edcc1
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=snapspare-edcc1.firebasestorage.app
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=461645762801
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:461645762801:web:27cf258e56095adf4e1950
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-Y6VCPEW6DF

VITE_USE_EMULATORS=false
